# TripoSR Environment Setup — Process Log

**Goal:** Run TripoSR (single-image → triplane → NeRF → mesh) locally with RTX 3050, with GPU-accelerated mesh extraction via `torchmcubes`.

**Status:** ✅ Working — image → textured mesh pipeline runs end-to-end.

---

## Final Environment Summary

| Component | Version | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| Python | 3.10.13 | via conda |
| conda env name | `2d_to_3d` | |
| PyTorch | 2.1.2+cu118 | pinned — do not let this drift |
| CUDA (runtime, PyTorch-matched) | 11.8 | standalone NVIDIA installer, **not** conda |
| CUDA compiler toolchain | NVIDIA CUDA 11.8 standalone install | `C:\Program Files\NVIDIA GPU Computing Toolkit\CUDA\v11.8\` |
| MSVC compiler | VS2022 Build Tools, older v143 subversion (~14.36) | pinned via `-vcvars_ver` flag |
| numpy | <2.0 (currently 1.26.4) | must stay pinned — torch 2.1.2 breaks on numpy 2.x |
| torchmcubes | 0.1.0, built from source with CUDA support | the main blocker of this whole process |

