## Setup Steps (in order)

### 1. Conda environment
```powershell
conda create -n 2d_to_3d python=3.10.13 -y
conda activate 2d_to_3d
```

### 2. PyTorch (CUDA 11.8 build, via pip)
```powershell
pip install torch==2.1.2 torchvision==0.16.2 torchaudio==2.1.2 --index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cu118
```

### 3. numpy pin
```powershell
pip install "numpy<2"
```

### 4. CUDA 11.8 Toolkit — standalone installer (NOT conda)
Downloaded from: `https://developer.nvidia.com/cuda-11-8-0-download-archive`
- Custom install
- Unchecked: Display Driver, NVIDIA GeForce Experience components, PhysX
- Kept: CUDA (Development, Runtime, Visual Studio Integration)
- Default install path used: `C:\Program Files\NVIDIA GPU Computing Toolkit\CUDA\v11.8\`

### 5. VS2022 Build Tools
Installed via `https://aka.ms/vs/17/release/vs_buildtools.exe`
- Workload: "Desktop development with C++"
- **Note:** the default install pulled the *latest* MSVC v143 subversion (14.44), which turned out to be too new for CUDA 11.8 (see Issue #5 below). An older v143 subversion (~14.36) was added via Individual Components and pinned explicitly at build time.

### 6. TripoSR repo
```powershell
git clone https://github.com/VAST-AI-Research/TripoSR.git
cd TripoSR
```

### 7. Dependencies (installed incrementally, see issues below for why)
```powershell
pip install rembg onnxruntime trimesh einops xatlas omegaconf transformers==4.35.0 huggingface_hub Pillow imageio[ffmpeg] gradio moderngl
```

### 8. torchmcubes (built from source, CUDA-enabled)
```powershell
# In a shell with VS2022 dev environment loaded (older MSVC pinned) + conda env active:
$env:PATH = "C:\Program Files\NVIDIA GPU Computing Toolkit\CUDA\v11.8\bin;" + $env:PATH
$env:CUDACXX = "C:\Program Files\NVIDIA GPU Computing Toolkit\CUDA\v11.8\bin\nvcc.exe"
$env:CMAKE_GENERATOR = "Ninja"
$env:NVCC_APPEND_FLAGS = "-allow-unsupported-compiler"
pip install git+https://github.com/tatsy/torchmcubes.git --no-cache-dir --force-reinstall
```

### 9. Re-pin torch after torchmcubes install (see Issue #6)
```powershell
pip install torch==2.1.2 torchvision==0.16.2 torchaudio==2.1.2 --index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cu118 --force-reinstall
pip install "numpy<2" --force-reinstall
```

### 10. Run inference
```powershell
python run.py examples/chair.png --output-dir output/ --bake-texture
```

